    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d1046">

                <pb facs="1291" n="1273" sameAs="frus:frus1946v11/pg1273"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">833.34/5–1346</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Uruguay</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Dawson</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                        State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left"><hi rendition="#small-caps">secret</hi></seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Montevideo</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1946-05-13T12:00:00-03:00">May 13, 1946—noon.</date><lb/>[Received
                        12:05 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>287. Embtel 284, May 10.<anchor n="7" xml:id="d1046-f1"/> In informal
                    conversation yesterday President<anchor n="8" xml:id="d1046-f2"/> mentioned
                    purchase of Canadian frigate saying he hoped our Government perceived no
                    objection. He even intimated that if we objected, matter would be reconsidered.
                    However, he made it clear he considers purchase very advantageous and would be
                    keenly disappointed if deal fell through.</p>
                <p>While President did not ask me to consult Department, I should appreciate its
                    views in case he reverts to matter.</p>
                <p>Naval Attaché<anchor n="9" xml:id="d1046-f3"/> reports Uruguayan Navy strongly
                    desires prompt purchase Canadian vessel in question and turned to Canada only
                    after applying unsuccessfully to US.<anchor n="10" xml:id="d1046-f4"/></p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Dawson</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d1046-f1" n="7" xml:id="d1046-f1-content">
                <p>Not printed.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d1046-f2" n="8" xml:id="d1046-f2-content">
                <p>Juan José Amezaga.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d1046-f3" n="9" xml:id="d1046-f3-content">
                <p>Capt. Forrest Tucker.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d1046-f4" n="10" xml:id="d1046-f4-content">
                <p>In telegram 192, May 17, 1946, to Montevideo, the Department indicated
                    acquiescence in this purchase (833.34/5–1346).</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
